WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.700
Point a telescope at the night sky.

2
00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:05.220
There is a faint smudge of light.

3
00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:10.270
It could be a comet, a small body of
ice and dust inside our Solar System.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.910
Or it could be a whole
galaxy of billions of stars,

5
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.990
vastly further away.

6
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.260
Nobody can fly there to check.

7
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:21.630
So how do astronomers work
out what they are looking at?

8
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.060
In this mission, you'll meet
the objects that fill the sky,

9
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:29.720
from comets to galaxies, and see
how they fit inside one another.

10
00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:35.440
Then you'll see how one cloud of gas and
dust can give four very different pictures.

11
00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:40.830
Your mission: find out how astronomers
decide what a smudge of light really is.
